==Latin==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ef/|lang=la}}

===Noun===
{{head|la|noun|head=ef|{{l|en|indeclinable}}}}

# {{non-gloss definition|The name of the letter ''{{l|la|F}}''.}}

====Usage notes====
* Multiple Latin names for the letter {{term||F|lang=la}}, {{term||f|lang=la}} have been suggested. The most common is {{term||ef|lang=la}} or a {{l|en|syllabic}} {{term||f|lang=la}}, although there is some evidence which also supports, as names for the letter, {{term||fē|lang=la}}, {{term||əf|lang=la}}, {{term||fə|lang=la}}, and even (in the fourth- or fifth-century first Antinoë papyrus, which gives Greek transliterations of the Latin names of the Roman alphabet’s letters) {{term|ιφφε|lang=grc}}.

====Coordinate terms====
* {{Latin letter names of the Roman alphabet}}

===References===
* Arthur E. Gordon, ''The Letter Names of the Latin Alphabet'' ([[w:University of California Press|University of California Press]], 1973; volume 9 of ''University of California Publications: Classical Studies''), especially pages 30–31, 42–44, and 63

